    "problemStatement": "Chef has a circular array AAA of NNN integers A1,A2…ANA_1, A_2 \\ldots A_NA1​,A2​…AN​ where ANA_NAN​ and A1A_1A1​ are considered adjacent.\n\nThe subarray Ai,jA_{i,j}Ai,j​ defined as an array formed using elements of AAA from ithi^{th}ith index element to jthj^{th}jth index element (both inclusive). Formally, Ai,jA_{i, j}Ai,j​ is defined as:\n\n\nIf i≤ji \\leq ji≤j, then the subarray of AAA from the index iii to index jjj, both inclusive.\nIf i&gt;ji &gt; ji&gt;j, then it denotes the subarray of AAA from index iii to index NNN, followed by subarray of AAA from index 111 to index jjj.\nA function f(B)f(B)f(B) is defined on an array BBB as the number of subarrays of BBB which have sum less than KKK.\n\nLet S=∑i=1N∑j=1Nf(Ai,j)S = \\sum_{i = 1}^N \\sum_{j = 1}^N f(A_{i, j})S=∑i=1N​∑j=1N​f(Ai,j​). Find the value of SSS modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two integers NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n###Output:\r\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the value of SSS modulo 1,000,000,0071,000,000,0071,000,000,007.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤101 \\le T \\le 101≤T≤10\n1≤N≤2∗1051 \\le N \\le 2*10^51≤N≤2∗105\n∣K∣≤1015|K| \\le 10^{15}∣K∣≤1015\n∣Ai∣≤109|A_i| \\le 10^9∣Ai​∣≤109 for each valid iii\n###Sample Input:\n\n`3\r\n3 1\r\n0 0 0\r\n2 1\r\n1 -1\r\n1 1\r\n-1\n`###Sample Output:\n\n`30\r\n5\r\n1\n`###Explanation\r\nIn the second test case, the array is [1,−1][1, -1][1,−1] and K=1K = 1K=1.\n\nf(A1,1)=0f(A_{1, 1})= 0f(A1,1​)=0\n\nf(A1,2)=2f(A_{1, 2}) = 2f(A1,2​)=2, because both the subarrays [1,−1][1, -1][1,−1] and [−1][-1][−1] have sum &lt;K&lt; K&lt;K.\n\nf(A2,1)=2f(A_{2, 1}) = 2f(A2,1​)=2, because the array we are considering now is [−1,1][-1, 1][−1,1], and both the subarrays [1,−1][1, -1][1,−1] and [−1][-1][−1] have sum &lt;K&lt; K&lt;K.\n\nf(A2,2)=1f(A_{2, 2}) = 1f(A2,2​)=1\n\nThe sum of these is 5, which is the answer.",
